@page "/docs/components/color-picker"
@using Blaizio.Docs.Examples.ColorPicker
<PageTitle>Color Picker - Blaizio</PageTitle>

<div class="typeset typeset-docs space-y-10">
    <header class="docs-page-header space-y-2.5">
        <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2">
            <h1 class="text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight">Color Picker</h1>
            <DocBadges Slug="color-picker" />
        </div>
        <p>A composable color picker: saturation/value area, hue and alpha sliders, text input, preset swatches and palettes, image sampling, gradients, and a native eye dropper. Reads and writes ten color formats, or a CSS gradient paint. Dragging needs an interactive render mode.</p>
    </header>

    <UsageBlock Example="typeof(ColorPickerUsageExample)" />

    <ExamplesHeading />

    <Demo Title="Alpha"
          Description="ShowAlpha adds the transparency slider and serializes alpha - here in the rgb format."
          Example="typeof(ColorPickerAlphaExample)" />

    <Demo Title="Formats"
          Description="Ten formats: HEX, RGB, RGBA, HSL, HSLA, HSB, HWB, CMYK, OKLCH and OKLab. Hex keeps a free-text field that accepts ANY format (even without the #) and converts; every other format renders per-channel fields - edit one number without retyping the string. These fields are also the precise, accessible path to an exact color: the area thumb is a keyboard-steppable 2D slider that announces saturation and brightness percentages (rename the axes via XAxisLabel / YAxisLabel on BzColorArea), but screen-reader users get exact values through the numeric channels."
          Example="typeof(ColorPickerFormatsExample)" />

    <Demo Title="Format dropdown"
          Description="ShowFormatPicker adds the dropdown; switching it converts the current value into the chosen format and re-emits it. Bind Format to follow along."
          Example="typeof(ColorPickerFormatPickerExample)" />

    <Demo Title="Saved colors"
          Description="ShowSaved adds the saved panel: the plus banks the current color, clicking a saved swatch applies it, the corner x removes it. Bind SavedColors to persist the list."
          Example="typeof(ColorPickerSavedExample)" />

    <Demo Title="Sizes" Description="Three width presets; pass your own width utilities via Class for anything else." Example="typeof(ColorPickerSizesExample)" />

    <Demo Title="Swatches"
          Description="Preset colors as one-click swatches; the one matching the current color marks itself selected."
          Example="typeof(ColorPickerSwatchesExample)" />

    <Demo Title="Surfaces"
          Description="Solid, Gradient and Image share one switch. Each is optional - ShowSolid, ShowGradient, ShowImage - the switch appears once more than one is on, and a picker with all three off still picks a solid color. Value is the CSS paint for whichever surface is active: a color string on Solid, a linear / radial / angular / diamond gradient on Gradient, and url(...) on Image. Bind Gradient and Image for the models behind those strings - the image grade is a filter, a separate CSS property, so it only travels on the model."
          Example="typeof(ColorPickerSurfacesExample)" />

    <Demo Title="Palette"
          Description="BzColorPalette lays presets out as named ramps - a label per row, shades stretched to line up column by column. Pass Groups, or compose BzColorPaletteGroup children."
          Example="typeof(ColorPickerPaletteExample)" />

    <Demo Title="Composed"
          Description="Drop the parts into ChildContent to build your own layout - anything from a minimal area-plus-hue pair to a full panel."
          Example="typeof(ColorPickerComposedExample)" />

    <Demo Title="Minimal"
          Description="Two parts and nothing else. The root is the state owner, so any subset of the parts is a working picker."
          Example="typeof(ColorPickerMinimalExample)" />

    <Demo Title="Hue only"
          Description="Same idea taken further: one slider, driving the whole color."
          Example="typeof(ColorPickerHueOnlyExample)" />

    <Demo Title="Opacity only"
          Description="A fixed color whose transparency is the only thing on offer - the alpha slider paired with its numeric field."
          Example="typeof(ColorPickerOpacityOnlyExample)" />

    <Demo Title="In a popover"
          Description="The classic picker button: a swatch trigger via RenderAs, the picker inside BzPopoverContent."
          Example="typeof(ColorPickerPopoverExample)" />

    <Demo Title="Eye dropper"
          Description="ShowEyeDropper adds the native EyeDropper pipette where the browser supports it."
          Example="typeof(ColorPickerEyeDropperExample)" />

    <Demo Title="Commit"
          Description="ValueChanged streams every pointer move; OnValueCommit fires once per settled interaction - persist there."
          Example="typeof(ColorPickerCommitExample)" />

    <Demo Title="Live preview" Description="Bind the picked color straight into styles." Example="typeof(ColorPickerLiveExample)" />

    <Demo Title="Disabled" Example="typeof(ColorPickerDisabledExample)" />
</div>
